title: 'fix(xcm): charge precise barrier-check weight on barrier rejection'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    When a barrier rejects an XCM, the executor previously reported the full message weight as
    `used`, over-estimating the work actually done. This adds an optional
    `WeightBounds::barrier_check_weight()` hook (default `None`): when a weigher provides it, the
    executor charges that precise weight on barrier rejection; otherwise it falls back to the
    previous full-message-weight behaviour, so existing `XcmConfig`s are unaffected.

    A `barrier_check` benchmark is added to `pallet_xcm_benchmarks::generic` (driven by a new
    `worst_case_barrier_check()` config method) to measure that weight. Westend and the Westend
    system parachains (Asset Hub, Bridge Hub, Collectives, Coretime, People) wire their executor
    `Weigher` to report the benchmarked value.

    Closes #7965.
crates:
- name: staging-xcm-executor
  bump: minor
- name: staging-xcm-builder
  bump: none
- name: pallet-xcm-benchmarks
  bump: minor
- name: parachains-common
  bump: patch
- name: bridge-hub-common
  bump: patch
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
